[_combine_similar_docs] docs:
['Convergent evolution is best exemplified by the similarity between the pectoral fins of fish and the front legs of cats. Both evolved independently to perform similar functions. This example illustrates how different species can develop similar traits in response to similar environmental pressures.', 'Convergent evolution is best exemplified by the pectoral fins of fish and the front legs of cats, as both have evolved to perform similar functions despite being anatomically distinct. This similarity is an example of evolutionary convergence, where different species develop similar traits in response to similar environmental pressures.', 'Convergent evolution is best exemplified by the similarity between the pectoral fins of fish and the front legs of cats, despite being very different species. This occurs when unrelated species develop similar traits in response to similar environmental pressures.', 'Convergent evolution is best exemplified by the similarities between the pectoral fins of fish and the front legs of cats. This occurs when different species develop similar traits in response to similar environmental pressures, despite being unrelated.']
