t legs of cats, showing similar function despite different origins. This similarity arose independently in each group.', 'Key information: Ichthyosaurs were aquatic dinosaurs with dorsal fins and tails, similar to fish. Their closest relatives were terrestrial reptiles without these features. The similarity in dorsal fins and tails between ichthyosaurs and fish is an example of homologous structures.', 'Convergent evolution is best exemplified by the pectoral fins of whales and the front legs of cats.', 'The key information is:Convergent evolution occurs when two unrelated species evolve to become more similar due to similar environmental pressures. This results in similar traits, but not necessarily a common ancestry.']
