['Here is the key information in 2 concise sentences:Two genes, B and E, determine coat color in Labrador retrievers, with B coding for black fur and E coding for yellow fur. The combination BBee results in brown fur, as E is dominant over the absence of E.', 'A Labrador retriever with the genotype BbEe will have a brown coat. This is because B codes for black fur, but is masked by the epistatic allele e. The e allele causes the fur to be yellow if E is not present, but since E is present, the fur will be brown due to the interaction of E and b.', 'Here is the key information in 2 concise sentences:Two genes (B and E) determine coat color in Labrador retrievers. The genotype BbEe results in brown fur due to the interaction of the two genes.', 'Here is the key information:Two genes (B and E) determine coat color in Labrador retrievers. The genotype BbEe results in brown fur.', 'Here is the key information in 2 concise sentences:Two genes determine Labrador retriever coat color: one codes for melanin (B or b) and the other for pigment deposition (E or e). The dominant allele E, when not present, results in yellow fur, while BBee results in brown fur.', 'Two genes (B and E) determine coat color in Labradors: B codes for black, b for brown, and E codes for yellow if not dominant. The genotype BbEe results in a brown coat.', 'Here is the key information in 2 concise sentences:Two genes determine coat color in Labrador retrievers: B for melanin and E for pigment deposition. The combination [BBEe] results in brown fur, as the dominant E allele is present.', 'Two genes determine Labrador retriever coat color: B (black) and E (pigment deposition). The combination BbEe results in brown fur.', 'Here is the key information in 2 concise sentences:Two genes (B and E) determine coat color in Labrador retrievers. The combination BbEe will result in a brown coat, regardless of the interaction between the genes.', 'Two genes determine coat color in Labradors: B and E. The combination BBee results in yellow fur.', 'Here is the key information in under 3 concise sentences:Two genes determine coat color in Labrador retrievers: one for melanin (B and b) and one for pigment deposition (E and e). The E allele is epistatic, meaning it determines fur color regardless of the B and b alleles. The genotype BBEe results in a brown coat.', 'Here is the key information in 2 concise sentences:Two genes (B and E) determine coat color in Labrador retrievers: one codes for melanin presence (B/b) and the other for pigment deposition (E/e). The combination BbEe results in a brown coat.', 'Here is the key information in under 3 concise sentences:Two genes (B and E) determine coat color in Labradors. The B gene codes for black fur, while the E gene is epistatic and determines whether fur is yellow or black/brown. The genotype BbEe results in brown fur.']
