 BBee results in yellow fur.', 'Here is the key information in under 3 concise sentences:Two genes determine coat color in Labrador retrievers: one for melanin (B and b) and one for pigment deposition (E and e). The E allele is epistatic, meaning it determines fur color regardless of the B and b alleles. The genotype BBEe results in a brown coat.', 'Here is the key information in 2 concise sentences:Two genes (B and E) determine coat color in Labrador retrievers: one codes for melanin presence (B/b) and the other for pigment deposition (E/e). The combination BbEe results in a brown coat.', 'Here is the key information in under 3 concise sentences:Two genes (B and E) determine coat color in Labradors. The B gene codes for black fur, while the E gene is epistatic and determines whether fur is yellow or black/brown. The genotype BbEe results in brown fur.']
