A single nucleotide substitution in the first codon position of the start codon (AUG) has the greatest potential for a deleterious effect, as it can lead to a premature stop codon, a truncated protein, and a complete loss of protein function. This is because the first position determines the amino acid identity and altering it can disrupt translation initiation, potentially disrupting the entire reading frame of the protein.
