During glycolysis, pyruvate is converted to lactate in the forward direction. In fermentation, lactate is converted back to pyruvate in the reverse direction. This is because in glycolysis, pyruvate is converted to lactate to produce NADH, whereas in fermentation, lactate is converted back to pyruvate.
