Two genes, B and E, determine coat color in Labrador retrievers. The B gene codes for black or brown fur, while the E gene codes for pigment deposition. The dominant allele B and E can result in black or yellow fur, respectively, while the recessive alleles b and e can result in brown or yellow fur, respectively. The genotype BBee or BbEe will result in a brown coat, as E is dominant and codes for yellow fur unless paired with e.
