The S phase is the part of the cell cycle where the quantity of DNA in a eukaryotic cell doubles, occurring as the cell replicates its DNA in preparation for cell division. This phase is crucial for cell division and DNA replication, and it occurs between the G1 and G2 phases, during which the genetic material is replicated.
