The S phase is the cell cycle phase where the quantity of DNA in a eukaryotic cell typically doubles. This occurs as the cell replicates its DNA in preparation for cell division, and it is crucial for both cell division and DNA replication. The S phase occurs between the G1 and G2 phases during interphase of the cell cycle, and it is the phase where genetic material is replicated.
