re intense and destructive fires by removing dead and decaying plant matter.', 'The most likely benefit of periodic natural wildfires in some forest ecosystems is that they remove dead and decaying plant matter, which reduces the risk of intense and destructive fires. This process is called prescribed burning.', 'The most likely benefit of periodic natural wildfires in some forest ecosystems is reducing the risk of more intense and destructive fires.', 'The most likely benefit of periodic natural wildfires in some forest ecosystems is reducing the risk of intense and destructive fires.', 'The most likely benefit of periodic natural wildfires is reducing the risk of intense and destructive fires by removing dead and decaying plant matter.']
